group index
note The in-memory shape of the auto layer: what an indexed repo is. One Index per process holds one File per text file under the root, each File holds its lines, its per-line colour spans, its imports and its Symbols, and each Symbol holds the raw material for xrefs plus the resolved callee and caller lists. Nothing here is persisted as truth: the whole thing is rebuilt from disk and the cache at startup. Symbols are addressed by SymRef, a pair of indices, which is fast but only valid until the next re-index; anything that has to survive one uses the (file path, symbol name) key instead.

